summary:
  A station's address is rewritten in a schedule while that schedule is being
  recorded, and the running capture keeps the entry's old filing.

history:
  An occurrence is filed under address@time. When a healed station moved, the
  schedule got the new address and the capture in progress kept the old key:
  the next tick called its own recording "skipped", the finished capture found
  no entry to settle, and a one-off stayed in the list to be called missed
  when its window closed. Found 2026-11-10 on the bench, before any release
  that moves an address mid-capture.

target:
  package/contents/ui/RecordingEngine.qml

find:
          if (_recActiveSchedKey === was) _recActiveSchedKey = key;

replace:
          if (_recActiveSchedKey === key) _recActiveSchedKey = was;

expect:
  Killed by tests/qml/tst_recordingengine.qml::test_a_station_moved_mid_capture_is_still_the_captures_own
  and tests/qml/tst_recordingengine.qml::test_a_capture_stopped_by_hand_after_the_move_spends_its_entry.
  Line-neutral.
